MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Believe feels like a natural next choice after Ten Thousand Fists because I want more of Disturbed's forceful vocals and heavy grooves.",
    "The End of Heartache strongly fits what I enjoy about In Flames and Soilwork: aggressive riffs with melodic passages. City of Evil and Hypnotize also offer the energy and adventurous melodies I want right now."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Let It Enfold You feels off because its emo and post-hardcore direction does not give me the groove and melodic metal combination I am looking for today.",
    "Fallen, The Open Door, and Smile Empty Soul fit parts of my listening history, but their melodic rock appeal is less compelling while I want something more aggressive."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Heavy guitars and melodic vocals alone seem to count too much as a match; the rhythm, vocal delivery, and balance of aggression and melody matter to me.",
    "My earlier interest in alternative rock seems to carry too much weight for what I want now, even though those albums still fit my broader taste."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent interest in Ten Thousand Fists makes another Disturbed album especially appealing, beyond simply recommending more heavy music.",
    "My repeated listening to In Flames and Soilwork points toward a particular mix of intensity and melody. A heavier album like Death Magnetic interests me, but heaviness by itself does not make it my first choice."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in heavy, melodic music, but some miss my current preference for forceful grooves and aggression balanced with melody."
}
